# The scenes of the checking-outgoing-requests deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# checking-outgoing-requests.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in checking-outgoing-requests.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: add WireMock to the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/wiremock/" gradle/libs.versions.toml

## Scene 2: step 2, the test dependency
note "Step 2: add it as a test dependency of the lesson."
show lessons/checking-outgoing-requests/example/build.gradle.kts "/^dependencies/" "lesson build file" --zoom 10

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's refund client. It sends the amount in *pounds*, and no Idempotency-Key header."
show TodaysRefundClient 23 36 "today's refund client" --zoom 30

## Scene 4: the weak test
note "The *weak* test: a stand-in provider answers, and the test checks the answer was handled."
show RefundResponseTest 35 39 "the weak test" --zoom 38

## Scene 5: the strong test
note "The *strong* test: WireMock verifies the request the code really sent."
show RefundRequestTest 22 44 "the strong test" --zoom 22,26-27,38-43

## Scene 6: the request is wrong
note "Run the tests against today's code:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:checking-outgoing-requests:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The answer was handled. The request was wrong: no Idempotency-Key header, and 12.5 where the provider expects 1250 pence."

## Scene 7: the fixed client
note "The client that sends pence, and the Idempotency-Key header:"
show RefundClient 19 29 "the fixed client" --zoom 22-26
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:checking-outgoing-requests:test"
callout "The request is the one the provider expects: method, address, headers and body."
